// EXPECT-DIAG: assigned but the value is never read (dead store)
// EXPECT-NO-DIAG: declared but never used
// LEC-005 guard against over-correction of 42_...: a read-modify-write is a
// READ of the old value, but its RESULT can still be dead. Here `x`'s only
// uses are the `+=` itself, so the store `+=` makes is never read -- that one
// dead store is real and must still be reported (and the variable is not
// "never used": the `+=` reads it, so only one warning applies, not two).
fn main(): int {
    mut x: int = 1;
    x += 1;
    return 0;
}
